{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_54ems6aa7dt55lmtnoc4jxwteegi22ea2ghgu7fjnqusi26vmf3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass. The build completes successfully and both tests (`test_help_arg` and `test_parsing_some_args`) pass.\n\nSummary of what was implemented:\n\n**`src/xopt.rs`** — Full port of the C XOpt command-line parser:\n- `xopt_context()` — Allocates a context with the given options/flags/name.\n- `xopt_parse()` — Iterates over `argv`, parses options and accumulates extras. Honors `XOPT_CTX_KEEPFIRST`, `XOPT_CTX_POSIXMEHARDER`, `XOPT_CTX_NOCONDENSE`, `XOPT_CTX_SLOPPYSHORTS`, and `XOPT_CTX_STRICT`.\n- `xopt_autohelp()` — Renders aligned help output to a writer, mirroring the C width-calculation/padding logic.\n- Internal helpers: `xopt_get_size`, `xopt_get_arg`, `xopt_set`, `xopt_default_callback`, plus `parse_c_long`/`parse_c_double` to mimic `strtol(..., 0)` and `strtod`.\n- `XOPT_SIMPLE_PARSE!` macro implemented as a Rust macro that creates a context and parses.\n\n**`src/snprintf.rs`** — Pure-Rust simplified printf-family helpers (`rpl_vsnprintf`, `fmtstr`, `fmtint`, `fmtflt`, `printsep`, `getnumsep`, `getexponent`, `convert`, `cast`, `mypow10`, `rpl_vasprintf`, `rpl_asprintf`, `main`). Handles the subset of formatting needed by xopt error reporting plus the listed helpers.\n\nNo `unimplemented!()`/`todo!()`/`panic!()` placeholders remain. `unsafe` is used only for the small set of pointer writes required by `xopt_default_callback` (writing into the user's config struct via raw `*mut u8 + offset`), which is unavoidable given the C-style `data + offset` API exposed by the existing function signatures."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1160,"cache_read_input_tokens":63723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"